{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqeo3v9kn6i","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: sweep endpoint also needs agent reap, not just sweepStaleClaims","summary":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: The agent-registry reap (transition owning agent out of 'running' when its stale claim is released) was added to sweepStaleClaims in daemon.js, but the POST /sweep HTTP route (routes/meta.js, ~lines 57-74) duplicates the release loop independently — both its force and non-force branches call releaseClaim directly WITHOUT reaping the agent. So an operator-triggered or test-triggered /sweep releases the claim but leaves the agent stuck 'running', still inflating /summary agents.running. The pre-existing sweepStaleAgents() 60s interval (daemon.js ~657, marks not-vouchedLive running agents 'dead') will eventually catch it, so the count self-heals within a minute, but the lockstep guarantee the task wanted is NOT honored on the /sweep path. Fix: factor the reap into a shared reapAgent(agentId) helper and call it from all three releaseClaim sites (sweepStaleClaims + both /sweep branches). Minor: sweepStaleClaims reaps to state 'stale' while sweepStaleAgents reaps to 'dead' — both non-running so harmless, but inconsistent vocabulary.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T03:42:48.584Z","vec":[-0.039572227746248245,-0.045159149914979935,0.0050032841973006725,0.0028172284364700317,-0.010648094117641449,-0.05654451996088028,-0.021152639761567116,-0.048682067543268204,0.019090503454208374,0.05512049421668053,0.02137250453233719,0.006362322252243757,-0.041598640382289886,0.023929664865136147,0.037189844995737076,0.025257816538214684,0.021210383623838425,0.0026271422393620014,-0.029700446873903275,-0.009148228913545609,0.06468745321035385,0.01767067238688469,-0.017185421660542488,-0.02097959816455841,-0.027252772822976112,-0.032414793968200684,-0.10262035578489304,-0.05930405482649803,-0.01779497228562832,-0.01983523555099964,0.05566485598683357,0.059249594807624